#!/bin/sh
case "${1:-}" in
    prereqs) exit 0 ;;
esac
cat <<'GUIDE'

===============================================================================
                         DevOS storage recovery
===============================================================================
The system could not finish booting. This does not by itself identify a disk
permission problem. A missing drive, incorrect boot configuration, full disk,
filesystem damage or hardware I/O error can also cause this screen.

1. Record the error above and identify the drive using: blkid
2. Inspect recent kernel messages using: dmesg | tail -n 60
3. Boot the DevOS live USB to copy important files to a separate disk and
   inspect device health before choosing a filesystem-specific repair.

Do not force a damaged filesystem read-write, run recursive chmod/chown on /,
use btrfs check --repair, or clear filesystem logs as a general-purpose fix.
Btrfs log clearing can discard recent changes and needs a specific diagnosis.
This rescue shell already runs as root; sudo and apt are not available here.
===============================================================================
GUIDE
